steps.constraints:
[
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] ∈ ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS THEN policy MUST return (True, any message) – i.e., the call is always allowed."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND any of the required arguments {\"merchant_id\", \"mcc\", \"fund_pooling\", \"crawl_website_clean\", \"qualification_passed\", \"mcc_assigned\", \"risk_flags\", \"escalated_to_compliance\"} are missing (value is None) THEN policy MUST return (False, \"Missing required arguments for approval: [...]\" )."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND arguments[\"crawl_website_clean\"] == False THEN policy MUST return (False, \"Website content contains prohibited material.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND arguments[\"qualification_passed\"] == False THEN policy MUST return (False, \"Merchant qualification verification failed.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND arguments[\"mcc_assigned\"] == False THEN policy MUST return (False, \"MCC code has not been assigned for this merchant.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND arguments[\"risk_flags\"] is a non‑empty list AND arguments[\"escalated_to_compliance\"] == False THEN policy MUST return (False, \"Risk flags present but escalation to compliance has not been performed.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL AND arguments[\"crawl_website_clean\"] == True AND arguments[\"qualification_passed\"] == True AND arguments[\"mcc_assigned\"] == True AND (arguments[\"risk_flags\"] == [] OR arguments[\"escalated_to_compliance\"] == True) THEN policy MUST return (True, \"All verification steps completed; approval allowed.\")."
  },
  {
    "statement": "IF arguments[\"tool_name\"] is NOT in ALWAYS_ALLOWED_TOOLS AND NOT equal to HIGH_RISK_TOOL THEN policy MUST return (True, any message) – i.e., unrestricted tools are allowed by default."
  },
  {
    "statement": "POST‑CONDITION: IF policy returns True for a call where arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL THEN it is guaranteed that crawl_website_clean == True, qualification_passed == True, mcc_assigned == True, and (risk_flags == [] OR escalated_to_compliance == True)."
  },
  {
    "statement": "POST‑CONDITION: IF policy returns False for a call where arguments[\"tool_name\"] == HIGH_RISK_TOOL, the denial reason must correspond to the first violated pre‑condition in the order: missing arguments → website not clean → qualification failed → MCC not assigned → un‑escalated risk flags."
  }
]

The statements translate the security request into explicit, checkable IF‑THEN rules that the policy function enforces: always‑allowed tools are permitted, every required verification flag must be present and positive before `approve_onboarding` can succeed, risk flags demand prior escalation, and any violation leads to a deterministic denial. The post‑conditions capture what must hold whenever approval is granted.
